    <DataNode elementId="AT3G11945-MONOMER" textLabel="homogentisate solanesyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G11945-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This enzyme functions as a homogentisate prenyltransferase when expressed heterologously in membrane fractions of &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; with an enzymatic activity of 5 pmol min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; mg&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; protein |CITS: [16989822]|. This enzyme works best with homogentisate as a prenyl acceptor. Under initial experimental conditions, the protein seemed to have the highest activity with farnesyl diphosphate and geranylgeranyl diphosphate. However, the addition of of 0.12 mM n-dodecyl b-D-maltoside significantly increased the activity of the enzyme toward solanesyl diphosphate (SDP), most likely because this detergent solubilized the long chain SDP compound |CITS: [16989822]|. Based on studies of HST from &lt;i&gt;Chlamydomonas reinhardtii&lt;/i&gt;, spinach, and Arabidopsis, a model for the mechanism of this enzyme has been proposed. It is hypothesized the HST binds to prenyl diphosphate in distinct manners to form at least two alternative complexes that go on to react differently with homogentisate and prenylate it prior to or after it becomes decarboxylated. It is also supposed that the larger |FRAME: SOLANESYL-PYROPHOSPHATE SDP|substrate binds tightly and preferentially in the mode that favors prenylation with decarboxylation. |CITS: [20400515]|. Overexpression of this HST enzyme in Arabidopsis plants causes increased accumuation of plastoquinone-9 and, surprisingly, tocochromanols (primarily &amp;alpha;-tocopherol). While the former is likely due to the activity of HST with SDP, directly upstream of plastoquinone-9 biosynthesis, the effect of HST on tocopherol accumulation is hypothesized to be indirect |CITS: [16989822]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G11945-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33307, RXN-12698" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009941" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G11945.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G11945" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="17569077" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOR-ENV-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16989822" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_20400515" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G18950-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G18950-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G18950-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Over-expression of AtHPT (the gene encoding homogentisate phytyltransferase) in leaves and seeds of Arabidopsis increased tocopherol level in both tissues. It indicates that HPT activity is limiting for tocopherol biosynthesis in Arabidopsis|CITS: [12586887]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G18950-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-3405" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G18950.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G18950" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="11706191" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
