    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-3282" textLabel="MONOMER-3282" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-3282" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Expressing the enzyme in E.coli confirmed its methylation activity with both gamma- and delta-tocopherols. Beta-tocopherol is not a substrate which indicates the enzyme specifically methylates the C-5 position of the aromatic ring. Over expressing in Arabidopsis seeds changed tocopherol composition (increased alpha-tocopherol) but not total content.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-3282" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-22498, RXN-22497, RXN-3444, RXN-3443" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G64970.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="G-2362" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="9851934" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="36." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="33.8, 36." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightSeq" value="33.8" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_9851934" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12492478" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-3261" textLabel="MONOMER-3261" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-3261" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="435" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The vte3 mutant plants have a significant decrease in alpha and gamma-tocopherol content, and an increase of beta and delta-tocopherol content. It provided genetic evidence that the vte3 locus is responsible for the MPBQ methyltransferase activity and is involved in tocopherol biosynthesis. In addition, plastoquinone level is also significantly decreased in the vte3 mutants which indicates that vte3 is also involved in plastoquinone biosynthesis. Vte3 was expressed in E.coli and in-vitro assay demonstrated that it encodes the MPBQ/MSBQ methyltransferase and the enzyme uses both MPBQ and MSBQ as substrates.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-3261" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="MPBQ/MSBQ methyltransferase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-22132, RXN-12804, RXN-3421, RXN-3841" />
